{
  "title": "Template: PEV Cycle Manifest",
  "tags": [
    "pev-cycle"
  ],
  "meta": {
    "template_version": "1.1.0"
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "status",
      "heading": "Status",
      "content": "**Filled by:** Orchestrator — created at start, updated at every phase transition and at every gate.\n\nThis doc is the cycle's entry point. The cycle lives at `docs/pev/cycles/{cycle-id}/` as seven docs cloned from `.pev/templates/cycle/`: `manifest` (this doc), `architect`, `decisions`, `builder`, `review`, `audit` and `friction`. `.pev-state.json` records this doc's id as `cycle_doc_id` and `layout: \"directory\"`. Only this doc carries the status tag (`in-progress`, `completed`, `incomplete`), which the orchestrator sets when it clones the doc.\n\n**Example:**\n```\nPhase: builder\nLayout: directory\nBaseline SHA: abc1234def5678\nMain branch: main\nMain repo: /home/dev/project\nStarted: 2026-03-21T14:30:00Z\nCycle ID: pev-2026-03-21-add-history-filtering\nEntry baseline (worktree): 0 CONTENT_UPDATED / 0 NOT_FOUND / 12 LINKED_STALE. Main context: 12 LINKED_STALE — matched, env parity OK.\nMain failing tests: none\nResume at: Phase 4, task-3 (Builder incarnation 2); tasks 1-2 done\n\nPhase transitions:\n- planning: 2026-03-21T14:30:00Z — cycle created\n- builder: 2026-03-21T15:00:00Z — plan approved\n```\n\n**Instructions:** Update this section at every phase transition, appending each transition with its timestamp (`planning`, `builder`, `auditor`, `doc-review`, `merge`, `completed`). `Baseline SHA` is main's HEAD at cycle start; the cycle's diffs start there. `Main branch` and `Main repo` are inputs to the merge step.\n\n**`Resume at:`** names the step a fresh session picks the cycle up at, and what is left. Rewrite it at every gate, before presenting the gate, and before any stop, so a later session can carry the cycle on from this section alone. It reads `Resume at: done` once the cycle completes.\n\nThe **entry baseline**, the worktree's own `axiom_graph_check` result after provisioning and before any Builder work, is the left bracket. It is recorded here with main's counts as context and the classification of any gap between them (env divergence / pre-existing debt / structural); its node ids go in `baseline`. The right bracket, Phase 6's **pre-audit check** verdict (`clean` / `unexplained-drift`), is recorded in `change-set`. Together they make the cycle's staleness a verified delta and, with a passing Reviewer verdict (`PASS`/`PASS_WITH_CONCERNS`), license the Auditor's code/test blanket-clean. On completion the merge step adds `Completed:` and the `Final check:` line. On failure, set the phase to `incomplete` with the reason."
    },
    {
      "id": "request",
      "heading": "Request",
      "content": "**Filled by:** Orchestrator — at cycle start, in the `clone_doc` call.\n\n**Example:**\n```\nAdd a history endpoint that supports filtering by date range\n```\n\n**Instructions:** Paste the user's original `/pev-cycle` prompt verbatim. Do not summarize or rephrase."
    },
    {
      "id": "scope",
      "heading": "Scope",
      "content": "**Filled by:** Architect — during planning. This is the one section of `manifest` the Architect writes; the doc-scope hook allows it and nothing else here.\n\n**Example:**\n```\nModules affected: history subsystem (axiom_graph.history), MCP server (axiom_graph.mcp_server).\n\nScope decision: Single-feature change targeting the history subsystem.\n```\n\n**Instructions:** Describe the scope as a coarse boundary — which modules and subsystems are involved. Do NOT list per-function changes. State the scope decision: single-feature (targets one feature tree) or cross-cutting (3+ features → reference or propose ADR). The Auditor uses `axiom_graph_check` and the change-set to determine review scope empirically, not this list."
    },
    {
      "id": "change-set",
      "heading": "Change Set",
      "content": "**Filled by:** Orchestrator — in Phase 6, after main is synced into the branch and the pre-audit check has run, before the Auditor dispatch.\n\n**Example:**\n```\nPlanned nodes (from Architect scope):\n- {project_id}::axiom_graph.history::get_history_since\n- {project_id}::axiom_graph.mcp_server::axiom_graph_history\n\nActual files changed (from git diff --name-only {main_branch}...HEAD):\n- axiom_graph/history.py\n- axiom_graph/mcp_server.py\n- tests/test_history_filtering.py\n\nBrought in by the sync (git diff --name-only HEAD...{main_branch}, before the merge):\n- axiom_graph/cli.py\n\nMain's stale ids at the sync (drift_query on main's index): {project_id}::docs/features/history/prd::filters\n\nBuilder deviations:\n- None reported\n\nPre-audit check: clean (staleness explained by the entry baseline, the change-set and the sync)\n```\n\n**Instructions:** Construct this from: (1) the Architect's `manifest::scope` and `architect::affected-nodes`, (2) `git diff --name-only {main_branch}...HEAD` (three dots: the branch's own changes, leaving out main's changes the sync brought in), (3) the **sync list**: `git diff --name-only HEAD...{main_branch}`, run before the sync's `git merge` (afterwards HEAD contains main and the list is empty), the files main changed since the branch forked; write `none` when main had not moved, (4) **main's stale ids at the sync**, taken whenever the sync list is not `none`: `axiom_graph_drift_query(project_root=\"{main_repo_path}\", format=\"ids\")` against main's index, called from the worktree session (an MCP call, not git), paged while its header says more rows remain; ids in full, comma-separated, or `none`, (5) the deviations in the Builder's `builder::inc-N.task-M.manifest` entries, (6) the Phase 6 **pre-audit check verdict** (the right bracket): `clean`, or `unexplained-drift` plus the offending node ids. The Auditor reads this to categorize stale nodes as `expected` (in the branch's set), `sync-explained` (main's changes the sync brought in) vs `collateral` (in neither). One batched `mark_clean` clears a node as sync-explained only when its own status is `CONTENT_UPDATED`, its file is on the sync list and not among the branch's changed files, its id is not on main's stale-id list, and its `via=` names no node in the branch's changed files; every other node the sync touched is residual, decided per node, so main's own stale ids and the cycle's doc drift never clear in the batch. The Auditor's blanket-clean gate reads the verdict: a `clean` verdict plus a passing Reviewer verdict (`PASS`/`PASS_WITH_CONCERNS`) lets the Auditor trust the Reviewer's validation instead of re-confirming code/test nodes by hand."
    },
    {
      "id": "baseline",
      "heading": "Baseline",
      "content": "**Filled by:** Orchestrator — at cycle start (the manifest clone's `set_sections`), then by the merge step (steps 4 and 8). No agent writes it: the doc-scope hook denies every PEV agent the manifest except `scope`.\n\nThe cycle's staleness by node id. Counts can match while the nodes differ, so the merge step compares ids: main's stale ids just before the merge are the merge target, an id already stale at entry is never charged to the cycle, and only an id the merge added is residue.\n\n**Example:**\n```\nEntry baseline (worktree): 0 CONTENT_UPDATED / 0 NOT_FOUND / 2 LINKED_STALE. Main context: 2 LINKED_STALE — matched, env parity OK.\nEntry stale ids (worktree): {project_id}::docs/features/history/prd::filters, {project_id}::docs/features/history/prd::api\nPre-merge (main): 0 CONTENT_UPDATED / 0 NOT_FOUND / 2 LINKED_STALE\nPre-merge stale ids (main): {project_id}::docs/features/history/prd::filters, {project_id}::docs/features/history/prd::api\nFinal check: at main's pre-merge line\nFinal stale ids (main): {project_id}::docs/features/history/prd::filters, {project_id}::docs/features/history/prd::api\n```\n\n**Instructions:**\n- **Intake** (Phase 1, after the entry check, through the manifest clone's `set_sections`): the entry bracket's counts with main's counts as context, and the worktree's stale node ids, `axiom_graph_drift_query(project_root=\"{worktree_path}\", format=\"ids\")`, paged while its header says more rows remain.\n- **Merge step 4** (before the branch lands): `Pre-merge (main):` with main's `check` line and `Pre-merge stale ids (main):` with main's `drift_query` ids. Written in the worktree and committed on the branch, so they land with the merge.\n- **Merge step 8** (completion, on main): the `Final check:` line and `Final stale ids (main):`.\n\nWrite ids in full, comma-separated, or `none`. Append each later line with `axiom_graph_patch_section(anchor=\"$\")`; never rewrite an earlier one."
    },
    {
      "id": "fix-list",
      "heading": "Fix List",
      "content": "**Filled by:** Orchestrator — for each fix round the user approves, before the fix dispatch. No agent writes it.\n\nOne `round-N` subsection per approved round (`round-1`, `round-2`, …), added with `axiom_graph_add_section(parent_id=\"fix-list\")`. The template seeds none.\n\n**Example** (`round-1`):\n```\nSource: review::verdict (FAIL), approved 2026-03-21T16:10:00Z\n1. tests/test_history_filtering.py: no test for an empty date range (US-2). Add one.\n2. history.py get_history_since: the end date is exclusive; the story says inclusive. Fix it and test it.\nNot fixed: review concern 3 (naming), accepted at the gate.\n```\n\n**Instructions:** Write the round before dispatching the fix. Number each item, say where it comes from (the review verdict, a review shard's verdict, the audit's `needs_fix`, a doc review finding) and what done means, and list the concerns the user chose not to fix. The fix dispatch names the round's section id; the fix Builder and the re-reviewer cite items by number (`round-1 item 2`). A round is not edited after its dispatch: the next round is a new subsection."
    }
  ]
}
